WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.824
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:03.824 --> 00:00:05.750
MICHAEL AMES: Your
genome is probably

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.050
the single most identifying
unique thing about you.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.150
The goal of
personalized medicine

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:14.750
is about gathering as much data
as we can on people to help

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:16.215
us understand them better.

00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:18.590
KRISTY CROOKS: In the research
study through the Colorado

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:20.010
Center for
Personalized Medicine,

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.730
we're trying to leverage those
differences in our discoveries.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.590
For each patient who
undergoes genotyping,

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.380
we get about 2.1 million
pieces of genetic data.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.057
MICHAEL AMES: What we need is
the computational resources

00:00:30.057 --> 00:00:32.390
to make sure that we will
never run out of storage space

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:34.850
or that we will never
pay for storage space

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.500
that we're not using.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.360
Underlying all of
those challenges

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.800
are the questions of security.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.420
KRISTY CROOKS: It needs
to be stored somewhere

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.586
that is HIPAA compliant,
even if it's de-identified.

00:00:43.586 --> 00:00:45.230
MICHAEL AMES: And
our solution was

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:48.770
to move that data onto
Google Cloud Platform.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:51.650
It gave us a way that was cost
effective and highly scalable.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.600
And if that was all
it had given us,

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.160
we would have been
perfectly pleased.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.680
What we're finding is
that that partnership

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:00.800
is enabling us to drive to
the next level of innovation

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.570
and advanced analytics.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:04.489
Google BigQuery as
a data warehouse,

00:01:04.489 --> 00:01:05.600
that's our beating heart.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.970
We gather data from lots
of different places.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:10.220
We have to match
up patient records.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:12.980
That activity took about
eight hours to run.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:15.470
We re-implemented that
logic in Google BigQuery,

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.960
and it finishes now
in about 15 minutes.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.940
Through personalized
medicine, we

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:23.810
can give doctors tools to
make the best diagnoses

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:24.980
and treatment decisions.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.650
With Google Cloud Platform,
we are chasing down

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:29.990
every opportunity to
improve human health

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:32.360
by bringing this data
together and analyzing it

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:35.260
in ways that have never
been analyzed before.

